Buuz 2.0 uses two licensing rules, depending on where the code came from.

1. core/ (the buuz-core crate) is derived from the original Buuz by
   Odbayar Nyamtseren and is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 only.
   See core/LICENSE and core/NOTICE.

2. Everything else in this repository is new code, licensed under either of

     * Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE), or
     * MIT License (LICENSE-MIT)

   at your option. This is the same "MIT OR Apache-2.0" dual license used by
   most of the Rust ecosystem.

The NOTICE file must be kept with any redistribution that includes core/.
See docs/decisions/0004-license-mit-or-apache-for-new-code.md for the
reasoning.

SPDX summary:
  core/**    Apache-2.0
  all other  MIT OR Apache-2.0
